Hi,

I remember this issue coming up once before.  I think the solution was to construct the stack _first_, with the data list argument containing the data that is needed when calling inla.surv().  Then, when calling inla.surv(), you'd supply the contents of the corresponding vectors from the output of inla.stack.data().

If that doesn't work, a search in the r-inla-discussion list archive may help.

Finn

