no. sorry...

> 2. We use the SPDE approach to approximate the Gaussian Field x(s) on
> a mesh created using the inla.mesh.2d() function at location points of
> soil pollution observations. On the other hand, the additional spatial
> effect U_i in equation (2) is a BYM based on a neighbourhood structure
> of the municipalities. Is there a way to model on the same support
> both spatial effects (x(s) and U).

problem is that your data is (probably) aggregated on regional level,
and the Poisson model does not aggregate well, since

\sum\exp(x_i) != \exp\sum(x_i)

so its not clear what to do. Maybe Dan/Finn/Elias has suggestions...

H

