I don't think the BYM structure allows for a coherent change of
support formulation unless you use a data augmentation scheme (see the
work of Patrick Brown and collegues), but you can't do that with INLA.

A hacky solution would be to define the spatial effect for u_i as the
average of an SPDE model over the region. This can be done with
inla.spde.make.block.A.  But be careful: THIS IS NOT THE SAME AS THE
BYM.

D

